00:17:09.345 --> 00:17:12.625
The first one is that there's really no parking. If you look at the map,

00:17:13.425 --> 00:17:16.305
the green area is the preserve itself.

00:17:16.465 --> 00:17:18.625
And if you look at where it intersects

00:17:18.625 --> 00:17:25.890
Skinner Hill Road on the top, it's only got about 10 or 20 feet of frontage, something like that. Certainly not enough to park a car.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:33.810
The other challenge we were faced with is that right smack dab in the middle of the property, there's a pretty good sized wetland.

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:36.930
And that would largely prevent without

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.130
an extreme

00:17:38.695 --> 00:17:39.815
level of effort,

00:17:40.615 --> 00:17:44.295
a trail that would run from north to south through the property.

00:17:45.015 --> 00:17:52.295
You're probably aware the blue on that map is Town Of Andover open space land that you own because of

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.710
the Route 6 Expressway transfer to the town a couple years back.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.670
We looked at these two properties together,

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:05.990
and if they are considered together, if there was a collaborative effort between the town and Joshua's Trust,

00:18:06.605 --> 00:18:12.045
